    "it.basis": "What these figures are based on (as on {d})",
    "it.b1": "Rates (as on {d}), tax year 2026-27: new regime nil to ₹4 lakh, 5% to ₹8 lakh, 10% to ₹12 lakh, 15% to ₹16 lakh, 20% to ₹20 lakh, 25% to ₹24 lakh, 30% above; rebate so that income up to ₹12 lakh pays no tax, with marginal relief just above; standard deduction ₹75,000 on salary. Old regime: nil to ₹2.5 lakh (₹3 lakh at 60, ₹5 lakh at 80), 5% to ₹5 lakh, 20% to ₹10 lakh, 30% above; rebate ₹12,500 up to ₹5 lakh; standard deduction ₹50,000. These are the rates the Salary slip tool already uses; they were not re-read from the Finance Act in this build, so check them.",
    "it.b2": "Advance tax (Income-tax Act 2025, sections 403 to 408): due when the tax after TDS is ₹10,000 or more; 15% by 15 June, 45% by 15 September, 75% by 15 December, all by 15 March; a presumptive taxpayer pays all by 15 March; payment up to 31 March counts for the year; a resident aged 60 or more with no business income is exempt.",
    "it.b3": "Interest: section 424 (the old 234B) is 1% a month or part of a month on the shortfall when less than 90% of the tax was paid; section 425 (the old 234C) is 3% on the shortfall of each of the first three instalments (none if 12% was paid by 15 June and 36% by 15 September) and 1% on the March shortfall.",
    "it.b4": "The sections above were checked word by word on 15 Nov 2026 against the official text on the Income Tax Department's website (incometaxindia.gov.in). The printed Act decides.",
    "it.b5": "Book profit is not taxable profit: depreciation under the Act, disallowed expenses and the presumptive rules change it. Give this plan and the data sheet to your accountant.",
    "it.b6": "Not worked out: surcharge, capital gains at special rates, foreign tax relief, tax on income of a minor, and the interest on late filing.",
