    "app.limits": "Limits helper",
    "cp.intro": "Bills you owe to micro and small suppliers have a legal payment limit under section 15 of the MSMED Act, 2006: the days you agreed in writing (never more than 45), or 15 days if nothing is written. If you pay later than that, the amount is allowed as an expense only in the year you actually pay it (section 43B(h) of the Income-tax Act, 1961; section 37(2)(g) of the Income-tax Act, 2025 from 1 April 2026). Paying before the return due date does not help for these bills.",
